//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 88 - QUEUE ITEM 2 ON ATTACK 87: REGIME-CONDITIONED VERSION OF ATTACK 71's PIVOT-SPACING FLOOR.
//
// The stored scheduled prompt again describes a board state ("Attack 37, build its filter stack") more
// than eighty attacks stale, instructing "continue numbering after 37." THE DOCS OVERRIDE IT, AGAIN: Attack
// 37 closed on cost at Attack 41; the filter stack in progress is on Attack 66/68/82/83/87, and this cycle
// is BTC Attack 88 (next free number after Attack 87, the last entry on the board). Attack 87's own queue
// item 2 named the one remaining untried term-4 candidate on Attack 83: "the divergence's own TIME
// SEPARATION normalized by regime (distinct from Attack 71's raw bar-count spacing)." This build executes
// that item, before falling back to Attack 87's own queue item 3 (a genuinely new mechanism) if it fails.
//
// THE TERM, ARGUED FROM THE MECHANISM (LESSON 49, not from either half's dates). Attack 71 tested an
// UNCONDITIONAL 20-bar minimum spacing between the two pivot-low bars a bullish divergence compares, and it
// collapsed both halves decisively (trades cut 89->18 and 80->12, PF 1.565->1.081 and 1.131->0.883). Its own
// diagnosis: on this mechanism, divergence pairs that resolve QUICKLY are the majority of the edge, not
// noise -- "divergence pairs separated by more time are not more reliable, they are rarer." That diagnosis
// was measured on the WHOLE sample, not split by volatility regime. This build tests a narrower, genuinely
// different hypothesis: that quick-forming pivot pairs are only suspect evidence of a real divergence in an
// otherwise-CALM tape (little intrinsic reason for OBV to swing meaningfully bar-to-bar), and are NOT
// suspect when the market is already in an ELEVATED-volatility regime (fast order flow can legitimately
// produce a genuine divergence in a short bar-count window). The floor is therefore EXEMPTED, not resized,
// when `elevatedVol` (Attack 83's own ATR14/close-vs-its-200-bar-average regime descriptor, reused
// verbatim) is true -- the identical construction shape as Attack 83's own successful climax-exclusion
// term (`validClimax = not (isClimax and not elevatedVol)`), applied here to spacing instead of raw volume.
// Both the 20-bar threshold (Attack 71's own value) and the regime descriptor (Attack 83's own value) are
// reused unchanged -- nothing is invented or retuned for this test (LESSON 49).
//
// This DOES NOT touch bullDiv's OBV-magnitude clause (divMagOk, Attack 68), the climax-exclusion clause
// (validClimax, Attack 83), breakoutTrigger, rBig, or swingAmp -- it only adds a third, regime-conditioned
// clause alongside them, folded into the same pivot-low arming bar. Pine:
// `strategies/pine/attack88-obv-divergence-regime-conditioned-spacing-floor.pine`.
//
// AUDIT (one line per leg):
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - unchanged, rBig still gates by exclusion on rLong = close - lastPivLow.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - unchanged, slPx = lastPivLow, the confirmed divergence low.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY, unchanged; short leg remains a reported standing
//        asymmetry (Attack 64).
//   BINDING (E17) - bullDiv (now divMagOk AND validClimax AND spacingOk) AND breakoutTrigger AND rBig AND
//        swingOk all necessarily bind; spacingOk is a strict WIDENING relative to Attack 71's unconditional
//        floor (elevated-regime bars are exempted) and a strict NARROWING relative to Attack 83/no-spacing-
//        term (calm-regime bars now also need >=20-bar separation) -- it can only remove a SUBSET of what
//        Attack 71 removed, and only a subset of what Attack 83 currently keeps.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - barsBetween (bar-count time separation between the two pivot-low bars, a NEW
//        quantity not read by any existing clause) vs divMagOk (normalized OBV magnitude at those bars) vs
//        validClimax/elevatedVol (realized-volatility regime, REUSED verbatim from Attack 83 -- not a new
//        independent axis, an intentional shared gate exactly as Attack 87 also reused it) vs rBig (price
//        distance to lastPivLow) vs swingAmp (price swing) -- one genuinely new quantity (time separation)
//        layered onto four already-audited ones, sharing the regime descriptor by design, not by oversight.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - barsBetween and spacingOk are computed and folded into bullDiv on the
//        SAME bar and in the SAME if-block where bullDiv itself is re-derived (the pivot-low confirmation
//        bar), exactly as divMagOk and validClimax already do -- not a new same-bar setup/trigger
//        conjunction. breakoutTrigger remains a later, distinct bar.
//   OCCUPANCY (LESSONS 24/28/29) - pyramiding=1, flat check gates every entry, unchanged.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 42/43) - LONG at 100% equity; expect cascadeRatio 1 on both halves, confirmed
//        below.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// FREQUENCY ESTIMATE, REGISTERED BEFORE RUNNING (HARD LESSON 4): Attack 71 found that MOST divergence pairs
// on this mechanism resolve within 20 bars regardless of anything else measured, which is why its
// unconditional floor cut 79.78% (H1) and 85.0% (H2) of trades. This term only RESCUES the subset of those
// tight-spacing pairs that occur in an elevated-volatility regime -- it cannot rescue calm-regime tight
// pairs, which Attack 71's own diagnosis says are the bulk of the edge. Registering honestly: because the
// base mechanism (bullish OBV divergence + breakout) does not itself require or correlate strongly with
// elevated volatility at the PIVOT-LOW bar specifically (unlike the climax bars in Attack 82/83, which are
// close to breakout by construction), I expect only a MINORITY of Attack 83's surviving 88/79 trades to be
// exempted by `elevatedVol`, and therefore expect this term to still cut a LARGE fraction of trades on both
// halves -- pre-registering a 40-70% cut on each half, materially better than Attack 71's ~80-85% but still
// likely a decisive rather than marginal reduction. A cut inside that band that still passes RATCHET v2
// would mean the elevated-regime subset specifically concentrates the edge; a cut near or above Attack 71's
// own 80-85% would mean the regime split does not meaningfully separate the tight-spacing population and
// the axis is exhausted in every form tried.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17), READ AGAINST ATTACK 83 (BASE) ON BOTH HALVES:
//   * PF IMPROVES ON BOTH HALVES (RATCHET v2 clause 1), DD DOES NOT WORSEN (clause 2 allowance if PF gain >
//     0.02) ON BOTH, TRADES >= 30 ON BOTH (clause 3) -> KEPT as the new base for term 4, the stack closes at
//     four terms.
//   * IMPROVES ONE HALF, HURTS THE OTHER -> REJECTED, exactly Attack 67/69/70/71/82/87's fate, not averaged.
//   * COUNT CUT > 50% ON EITHER HALF -> a split-feasibility problem under clause 4, and per Attack 71's own
//     precedent this alone can decide the result before PF is even examined.
//   * TRADES BELOW ~30 ON EITHER HALF -> a direction, not a result (LESSON 12).
//   * EITHER WAY: if this is the third failed term-4 axis (after Attack 71 and Attack 87), the filter stack
//     on Attack 83 is CLOSED at three terms and the next cycle owes a genuinely new mechanism per Attack
//     87's own queue item 3.
//   REPORT GROSS, COMMISSION, ACHIEVED RATIO, AVG LOSER AND WIN RATE alongside net (LESSONS 36/39 and the
//     board's three-drawdown-category taxonomy).

strategy("BTC Attack88 OBV divergence regime-conditioned spacing floor", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

pivotLeft   = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation bars, left")
pivotRight  = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation bars, right")
minRpct     = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars     = input.int(192, "Max bars in trade")
obvRangeLen = input.int(200, "OBV normalizing range lookback")
divMagPct   = input.float(3.0, "Min OBV divergence magnitude, % of OBV's own range")
volAvgLen   = input.int(20, "Volume trailing average length (climax definition)")
climaxMult  = input.float(2.5, "Volume climax multiple of its own trailing average")
atrLen      = input.int(14, "ATR length (regime descriptor)")
regimeLen   = input.int(200, "Regime lookback for ATR/close's own average")
spacingMinBars = input.int(20, "Min bar spacing between pivot lows, calm regime only (Attack 71's own value)")

pl  = ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
ph  = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLeft, pivotRight)
obv = ta.obv

obvRange = ta.highest(obv, obvRangeLen) - ta.lowest(obv, obvRangeLen)

volAvg  = ta.sma(volume, volAvgLen)
isClimax = volume >= volAvg * climaxMult

atrPct       = ta.atr(atrLen) / close
atrPctAvg    = ta.sma(atrPct, regimeLen)
elevatedVol  = atrPct > atrPctAvg

var float lastPivLow    = na
var float prevPivLow    = na
var float lastPivLowOBV = na
var float prevPivLowOBV = na
var int   lastPivLowBar = na
var int   prevPivLowBar = na
var float lastPivHigh   = na
var bool  bullDiv       = false

if not na(pl)
    prevPivLow    := lastPivLow
    prevPivLowOBV := lastPivLowOBV
    prevPivLowBar := lastPivLowBar
    lastPivLow    := pl
    lastPivLowOBV := obv[pivotRight]
    lastPivLowBar := bar_index[pivotRight]
    if not na(prevPivLow)
        obvDivMag   = lastPivLowOBV - prevPivLowOBV
        divMagFloor = obvRange * divMagPct / 100
        divMagOk    = not na(obvRange) and obvDivMag > divMagFloor
        validClimax = not (isClimax and not elevatedVol)
        barsBetween = lastPivLowBar - prevPivLowBar
        spacingTooTight = barsBetween < spacingMinBars
        spacingOk   = not (spacingTooTight and not elevatedVol)
        bullDiv := lastPivLow < prevPivLow and obvDivMag > 0 and divMagOk and validClimax and spacingOk

if not na(ph)
    lastPivHigh := ph

rLong = not na(lastPivLow) ? close - lastPivLow : na
minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rBig  = not na(rLong) and rLong >= minR

breakoutTrigger = not na(lastPivHigh) and ta.crossover(close, lastPivHigh)

swingAmp = not na(lastPivHigh) and not na(lastPivLow) ? lastPivHigh - lastPivLow : na
swingOk  = not na(swingAmp) and swingAmp > 0

goLong = bullDiv and breakoutTrigger and rBig and swingOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := lastPivLow
    tpPx   := close + swingAmp
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(lastPivLow, title="LastPivotLow")
plot(lastPivHigh, title="LastPivotHigh")
